BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:impact-brazil@energyplanningweek.info
DTSTAMP:20261126T094143Z
DTSTART:20261202T081500Z
DTEND:20261202T090000Z
SUMMARY:EPW 2026: Impact session: Brazil's national energy plan and the LTE
 S Network
LOCATION:Auditorium\, GIZ Campus Forum\, Friedrich-Ebert-Allee 32\, 53113 B
 onn\, Germany
DESCRIPTION:Brazil's Energy Research Office presents the country's national
  energy planning instruments\, the long-term PNE 2055 and the ten-year exp
 ansion plan PDE 2035\, and reflects on how peer exchange through the LTES 
 Network informed national planning practice. An impact spotlight on what N
 etwork collaboration looks like for national planning processes.\n\nProvis
 ional programme\, check for changes: https://energyplanningweek.info/#impa
 ct-brazil
URL:https://energyplanningweek.info/#impact-brazil
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:session-4@energyplanningweek.info
DTSTAMP:20261126T094143Z
DTSTART:20261202T093000Z
DTEND:20261202T111500Z
SUMMARY:EPW 2026: Session 4: Planning under geopolitical uncertainty
LOCATION:Auditorium\, GIZ Campus Forum\, Friedrich-Ebert-Allee 32\, 53113 B
 onn\, Germany
DESCRIPTION:Geopolitical volatility\, fuel-price shocks and supply disrupti
 ons have moved energy security back to the centre of national planning. Th
 is session examines how countries stress-test scenarios against these risk
 s\, how the fossil-fuel transition and stranded-asset exposure are treated
  in national frameworks\, and how alternative plans are conceived to respo
 nd to supply disruptions.\n\nProvisional programme\, check for changes: ht
 tps://energyplanningweek.info/#session-4
URL:https://energyplanningweek.info/#session-4
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ai-showcase@energyplanningweek.info
DTSTAMP:20261126T094143Z
DTSTART:20261202T111500Z
DTEND:20261202T123000Z
SUMMARY:EPW 2026: Lunch session: state-of-the-art showcase of machine learn
 ing and artificial intelligence in energy planning
LOCATION:Auditorium\, GIZ Campus Forum\, Friedrich-Ebert-Allee 32\, 53113 B
 onn\, Germany
DESCRIPTION:A working-lunch showcase of applied AI uses prioritised by the 
 LTES Network – demand and load forecasting\, scenario development and se
 nsitivity analysis\, and data processing and quality assurance.\n\nProvisi
 onal programme\, check for changes: https://energyplanningweek.info/#ai-sh
 owcase
URL:https://energyplanningweek.info/#ai-showcase
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:session-5@energyplanningweek.info
DTSTAMP:20261126T094143Z
DTSTART:20261202T123000Z
DTEND:20261202T141500Z
SUMMARY:EPW 2026: Session 5: Climate risks and adaptation in national energ
 y scenarios
LOCATION:Auditorium\, GIZ Campus Forum\, Friedrich-Ebert-Allee 32\, 53113 B
 onn\, Germany
DESCRIPTION:Climate variability and physical risks – heatwaves\, floods\,
  droughts and shifting hydrology – are stress-testing national energy sy
 stems in real time. This session examines how planning teams incorporate c
 limate risks and adaptation into long-term scenarios: from El Niño-driven
  droughts in hydropower-dependent systems to cooling demand and flood expo
 sure\, and the data and methods needed to make plans resilient.\n\nProvisi
 onal programme\, check for changes: https://energyplanningweek.info/#sessi
 on-5
URL:https://energyplanningweek.info/#session-5
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:session-6@energyplanningweek.info
DTSTAMP:20261126T094143Z
DTSTART:20261202T144500Z
DTEND:20261202T163000Z
SUMMARY:EPW 2026: Session 6: Transformative methods\, transformative scenar
 ios?
LOCATION:Auditorium\, GIZ Campus Forum\, Friedrich-Ebert-Allee 32\, 53113 B
 onn\, Germany
DESCRIPTION:Scenario practice is evolving: deep uncertainty and robust deci
 sion-making\, agent-based and participatory modelling\, and open-source to
 ols are moving from research into government planning\, bringing new actor
 s and interdisciplinary insights into the scenario-building process itself
 . This session examines how these methods can be navigated within the real
 ities government planners face: resource constraints\, institutional manda
 tes and political viability.\n\nProvisional programme\, check for changes:
  https://energyplanningweek.info/#session-6
URL:https://energyplanningweek.info/#session-6
END:VEVENT
